# Repository Boundaries, Sync Separation & Artifact Lifecycle

Apply whenever reading, creating, or updating manga content inside `manga/`.

## Single-Manga-Per-Clone Architecture

- **One manga per cloned repository**: Manga Studio is a reusable template repository. Each manga series lives in its own independent Git repository cloned from the master template, with all manga-specific files organized inside `manga/`.
- **Master template protection**: The master `manga-studio` template repository must never contain a `manga/` directory, manga-specific stories, characters, artwork, or active huddle sessions. Only initialize `manga/` inside a cloned manga repository via `/new-manga` (or explicit creator confirmation).
- **Upstream sync hygiene**: Keep reusable studio infrastructure (`AGENTS.md`, `.cursor/agents/`, `.cursor/rules/` template rules, `.cursor/skills/`, `.cursor/commands/`, `templates/`, `docs/`) free of manga-specific plot or character data so clones can pull upstream template updates cleanly without merge conflicts. If a manga clone needs local-only Cursor rule tweaks, store them in `.cursor/rules/local-*.mdc`.

## Lifecycle & Versioning Rules

Production artifacts progress through four explicit states recorded in frontmatter or `manga/production/production-tracker.yaml`:
`draft` -> `ready-for-approval` -> `approved` -> `published`

- **Draft protection**: Exploratory production edits belong in `draft` files, `manga/art/concepts/`, or versioned filenames (`-v2`, `-v3`). Unapproved brainstorming belongs in `manga/creative/huddle-session.yaml` or `manga/creative/ideas/`.
- **No silent overwrites**: Never overwrite an `approved` or `published` character bible, reference sheet, chapter script, or edition export in place without explicit user authorization.
- **Provenance preservation**: When superseding an approved asset or decision, keep prior paths and IDs recorded in `manga/art/asset-log.yaml`, `manga/creative/decisions.yaml`, or `manga/production/decisions.md`.
